<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pier Luigi Farnese</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1503–1547</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pier Luigi Farnese was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii">Pope Paul III</a>, who created for him the Duchy of Castro in 1537 and the Duchy of Parma and Piacenza in 1545. His harsh rule over the Piacenza nobility made him enemies, and he was assassinated in 1547 in a conspiracy backed by the imperial governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. His descendants ruled Parma until 1731.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pier-luigi-farnese.jpg" alt="Pier Luigi Farnese" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pier_Luigi_Farnese_di_Tiziano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
